# Microwave Cacio E Pepe

Based on [Vegetables Unleashed Jose Andreas](https://www.amazon.com/Vegetables-Unleashed-Cookbook-Jose-Andres/dp/0062668382) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251113132913/https://www.amazon.com/Vegetables-Unleashed-Cookbook-Jose-Andres/dp/0062668382)), pg. 102

{ rating="3" image="microwave_cacio_e_pepe.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2 cup [elbow macaroni]{ ing="elbow-macaroni" }
- [ ] 6 cups [water]{ ing="water" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }
- [ ] 1 cup [frozen corn kernels]{ ing="frozen-corn-kernels" }, frozen peas, or fresh peas
- [ ] 4 Tbsp [butter]{ ing="butter" }
- [ ] 1 cup [grated Pecorino Romano]{ ing="grated-pecorino-romano" } or Parmigiano-Reggiano
- [ ] [Ground pepper]{ ing="ground-pepper" }

## Recipe

1. Combine pasta and [water]{ ing="water" } in a microwaveable bowl, add a pinch of [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }, and microwave on high for 5 min
1. Stir in the peas and return for 1 more minute
1. Working quickly, pour off most of the [water]{ ing="water" } until a few Tbsp remain
1. Vigorously stir in [butter]{ ing="butter" } and cheese. Caution to not stir too much or the cheese can ball up and not be evenly distributed
1. Serve with fresh [ground pepper]{ ing="ground-pepper" }

## Notes

1. The recipe is doubled
1. Can also be made by boiling pasta and adding the ingredients after
